The purpose of this section is to analyze the effect of the QND $S$-$R$ interaction on the evolution of the system's density matrix.
To this end, we first express the density matrix in terms of the system's eigenbasis.
Let $\{|n\rangle\}$ be the eigenbasis of $H_S$, such that $H_S |n\rangle = E_n |n\rangle$.
The density matrix $\rho^s(t)$ in this basis is given by:
\begin{equation}
\rho^s(t) = \sum_{n,m} \rho^s_{nm}(0) |n\rangle \langle m|.
\end{equation}
Substituting the expression for $\rho^s_{nm}(t)$ from Eq. (\ref{2g}) into the above equation, we get:
\begin{equation}
\rho^s(t) = e^{-{i \over \hbar}(E_n-E_m)t} e^{i(E^2_n-E^2_m) \eta(t)} e^{- (E_n-E_m)^2 \gamma(t)} \sum_{n,m} \rho^s_{nm}(0) |n\rangle \langle m|.

