\section{$H_F$ for the square pulse protocol}
Here we provide a detailed calculation of stroboscopic Floquet effective Hamiltonian ($H_F$) for the square pulse protocol using the Floquet-Magnus (F-M)
expansion in a rotating frame. The F-M method yields $H_F$ as a 
perturbative expansion in inverse drive frequency ($\tau$). However, transition to a 
rotating frame automatically ensures an infinite order resummation in $\tau$. Thus finally we get a series expansion of $H_F$ in inverse drive-amplitude ($1/\gamma_k$) where all the terms are resummed in $\tau$ \cite{asen, replica, anatoli1, anatoli2}. This extends the validity of $H_F$ to the low drive frequency regime but limits it to the high drive amplitude regime. The Hamiltonian for the driven system is given by, 
\begin{equation}
    H(t)=H_0+H_D(t)
\end{equation}
where $H_0=\sum_i(-1)^{i}S_i.S_{i+1}-h\sum_iS^z_i$ and we apply a local drive at the $k$-th site $H_D(t)=\gamma_k \textrm{Sgn}(\sin(\omega t))S^x_k$ with $\omega=2\pi/\tau$.

