In the following, the qualitative behavior of the critical chemical potential $v = (\beta\mu)_c$ in the RG description of the homogeneous Bose gas is worked out. It appears quite difficult to do this directly from Eqs.\ (\ref{flow1}) and (\ref{flowtG}). However, these equations can be simplified in a way which, on the one hand, does not modify the essential behavior of $v$ but, on the other hand, allows to investigate the dependence on ${\hat a}\equiv a/\lambda_T$ analytically. In a first step, we use that typically $M\ll E_>$ with $E_>=1/2$ the scaled cutoff energy, and neglect the $M$ dependence of the Bose-Einstein distribution $N_{BE}$ and of the denominator $2(E_>-M)$ which appears in Eq.\ (\ref{flowtG}). Furthermore, we disregard the nontrivial renormalization of $\tilde G$ at high energies due to two-body scattering and thus drop the term $-\tilde G^2 b/2E_>$ from Eq.\ (\ref{flowtG}). The relation between the initial condition for $\tilde G(l)$ and the scattering length ${\hat a}$ is then given by $\tilde G(0) = 8\pi^2{\hat a} /\sqrt{2\pi b(0)}$. The flow equations now read
\begin{eqnarray}
\label{flow11}\frac{dM}{dl}&=&2M- 2\frac{{\widetilde G}}{2\pi^2}bN_{BE},\\
\label{flowtG1}\frac{d{\widetilde G}}{dl}&=& {\widetilde G}-\frac{{\widetilde G}^2b}{2\pi^2}\left[4bN_{BE}(N_{BE}+1)  +\frac{N_{BE}}{E_>}\right]
\end{eqnarray}
with $N_{BE}=[\exp(b(l)E_>)-1]^{-1}$. In a second step, Eq.\ (\ref{flowtG1}) is simplified further by setting 
$$b(l)N_{BE}=\left\{ \begin{array}{cc} 
0 & \quad b(l)\ge 1, \\
1/E_> & \quad b(l)< 1.
\end{array}\right. $$ This modification, which has only a small effect on the flow of $\tilde G$, turns  Eq.\ (\ref{flowtG1}) into
\begin{equation}\label{flowG3}
\frac{d{\widetilde G}}{dl}=\left\{ \begin{array}{cc}
{\widetilde G} & \quad l\le \ln \sqrt{b(0)}, \\
{\widetilde G} -q {\widetilde G}^2 & \quad l > \ln\sqrt{b(0)}
\end{array}\right.
\end{equation}
where $q=20/2\pi^2$.

