The Laplace sum rules (LSR) are a powerful tool for extracting the spectral functions from experimental data and for constraining the QCD vacuum structure in the $V-A$ channel.
In this paper, we will apply the LSR to the ALEPH/OPAL data on the $V-A$ spectral functions and extract the relevant information on the QCD vacuum. The LSR are based on the relation between the hadronic and the photon propagator in the complex energy plane, which can be written as: 
\begin{equation*}
