\end{equation}
where the time-independent Hamiltonian $H_0 = \xi(\hat{\boldsymbol{p}}) + V_0(\boldsymbol{r})$ has eigenstates $\phi^j_{\boldsymbol{k}}(\boldsymbol{r})$, which are used to construct the Wannier functions. The Hamiltonian matrix elements in terms of Wannier functions can be written as
\begin{equation}
    \bra{w_{i\boldsymbol{R}'}}H\ket{w_{j\boldsymbol{R}}} = \bra{w_{i\boldsymbol{R}'}}H_0\ket{w_{j\boldsymbol{R}}} +  
